# Keep line endings LF in the repository.
#
# The history is already all-LF; this makes that explicit rather than leaving it
# dependent on each contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Git stores LF in blobs
# and converts in the working tree, so `text eol=lf` also asks for LF on
# checkout — which keeps a Windows worktree byte-identical to the blobs instead
# of round-tripping CRLF on the way in and out.
*               text=auto

# Explicit for sources and build files, so intent does not rest on Git's
# content heuristics.
*.scala         text eol=lf
*.sbt           text eol=lf
*.properties    text eol=lf
*.md            text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.json          text eol=lf
*.xml           text eol=lf
.gitignore      text eol=lf
.gitattributes  text eol=lf
